  "conditions": {
    "dedicated": true,
    "detail": "Only this SGLang server (and, for the speed and long-context rows, the small cache-busting proxy in front of it) was resident; the image server that normally runs on the box was stopped, and nvidia-smi listed no other compute process. The only other running container was a small host metrics exporter (python, about 10 MB, no GPU).",
    "isolation_check": "nvidia-smi compute apps -> 1579677, .venv/bin/python 1579734, sglang::scheduler ; docker ps -> 1 containers; load1 at start 1.02"
  },
  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Tool calling needs SGLang with the minicpm5 tool-call parser (sgl-project/sglang#25600). The openbmb cookbook says to install SGLang from main because v0.5.12.post1 lacked it; the PyPI 0.5.20 wheel used here ships it, so no source build is needed any more. The model writes XML tool calls (<function name=\"x\"><param name=\"k\">v</param></function>) and they come back as OpenAI tool_calls with finish_reason tool_calls, with thinking on and off."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "SGLang has no MiniCPM5 reasoning parser, but the model uses plain <think> ... </think>, so --reasoning-parser qwen3 splits it into reasoning_content. With enable_thinking left unset the template adds no <think> prefix; the model opens the tag itself and the qwen3 parser still catches it."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "flashinfer JIT-compiles its prefill kernels on the first request and shells out to ninja. In a venv that is not activated the first prefill dies with FileNotFoundError: ninja and the scheduler exits; put the venv bin directory on PATH before starting the server."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "In a llama.cpp deployment the card warns that the default min_p 0.05 causes repetition and asks for min_p 0; the SGLang default min_p is already 0."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Accuracy here is far below the same suite with thinking left on, and the gap was checked by hand before it was reported: it is a real loss, not a format or scorer artefact. Every miss inspected came back as a clean extracted answer in exactly the shape the suite expects - a bare option letter for the syllogism items, a bare name for the ordering items - two or three output tokens long, with nothing wrapped in tags and nothing stranded in reasoning_content. The model simply answers immediately and guesses. The same items, with thinking on, took 558-1,555 output tokens and came out right."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Thinking OFF row. On MiniCPM5 that means the chat template was rendered with enable_thinking=false, which prefills an empty think block instead of opening <think>; it goes out as chat_template_kwargs {\"enable_thinking\": false} on every request of the run and is recorded in this row's request block, which is why this row does not share its config_id with the thinking-on row of the pair. Nothing else differs: same server, same flags, temperature 0 and seed 42. The row exists because more than 10 % of the thinking-on row's items ran into the output budget: 15 of its 120 items hit the 2,048-token cap mid-thought, which scores them wrong however good the model is. Here that is 0 of 120, and accuracy moves 0.7833 -> 0.3333. The per-item spot-check behind that direction is the gotcha alongside this one. Read the pair together, never this row alone, and do not compare this number with a model that has no thinking mode to turn off."
    }
  ],
